{
  "abstract": "This corrected successor separates existence of the SPT-filtered Gaussian measure, finite-cutoff Borel summability, and removal of the cutoff. A positive proper-time gap makes the bounded-volume covariance trace class and gives all finite Sobolev moments. Nonnegative quartic finite-mode interactions are Borel summable with an exact positive-ray Borel-Laplace representation, and weighted convergence of Borel transforms is proved sufficient for cutoff removal. Selection and stability of the gravitational interaction, uniform constructive bounds, the physical removal limit, and BRST/BV reconstruction remain explicit gates.",
